{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data or Evaluator feedback, so this is a conservative baseline meant to finish the course and produce telemetry. Geometry: five line sensors spread evenly across the 0.08 m width (x = -0.04 to +0.04 m) at y = 0.04 m, ahead of the axle so steering reacts before the wheels reach a bend. A 12 mm footprint is used so the 25 mm tape is always covered by at least one sensor. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate turning response. Mass 0.8 kg keeps yaw inertia low. Controller: sensor weights are proportional to sensor x (-1, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 1), so the signal is a centroid estimate of the line position and is bounded to ±1. kp = 3 gives about 1050 PWM counts of differential per unit of signal, which is a firm but not aggressive correction. kd = 0.3 damps oscillation without amplifying sensor noise much. ki = 0.05 is small, since the line-centre bias is expected to be low. base_speed = 1.7 targets the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish under 3 s while leaving margin for the cornering slowdown. line_loss = last_direction keeps the robot turning toward the side it last saw the line. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with some oscillation on the slalom. The telemetry should show whether base_speed is too high (off-track or line-loss events on tight bends) or too low (failure to finish within 3 s), and whether kp is too low (large rms_error) or too high (large steering_oscillation).",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.7,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.05,
    "kd": 0.3,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "A conservative first candidate: five evenly spaced 12 mm sensors, base_speed 1.7, kp 3, kd 0.3, with a linear weight profile. No race data exists yet, so the values come from the contract's scale and the 1.5 m/s finish requirement, and the full telemetry set is requested to guide the next revision."
    }
  }
}
